{"name":"Black Swan","hex":"#332200","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black swan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Cygnus atratus, a swan with black plumage and a red bill which is endemic to Australia. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something believed impossible or not to exist, especially if an example is subsequently found; also, something extremely rare; a rara avis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black_swan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black swan","blocks":[{"text":"The black swan is a large waterbird, a species of swan which breeds mainly in the southeast and southwest regions of Australia. Within Australia, the black swan is nomadic, with erratic migration patterns dependent on climatic conditions. It is a large bird with black plumage and a red bill. It is a monogamous breeder, with both partners sharing incubation and cygnet-rearing duties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Black_swan_%28Cygnus_atratus%29_Scottsdale.jpg/330px-Black_swan_%28Cygnus_atratus%29_Scottsdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_swan","wikidata":"Q131044"},{"title":"Black Swan (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Black Swan is a 2010 American psychological horror thriller film directed by Darren Aronofsky, from a screenplay by Mark Heyman, John McLaughlin, and Andres Heinz, and based on a story by Heinz. Starring Natalie Portman, Vincent Cassel, Mila Kunis, Barbara Hershey, and Winona Ryder, the film follows a production of Tchaikovsky's Swan Lake by the company of New York City Ballet, led by Artistic Director Thomas Leroy (Cassel). The production requires a ballerina to play the innocent and fragile White Swan, for which the committed dancer Nina Sayers (Portman) is a perfect fit, as well as the dark and sensual Black Swan, which are qualities better embodied by the new rival Lily (Kunis). Nina is overwhelmed by immense pressure when she finds herself competing for the role, causing her to lose her tenuous grip on reality and descend into madness."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/68/Black_Swan_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Swan_(film)","wikidata":"Q180214"},{"title":"Swan","blocks":[{"text":"Swans are birds of the genus Cygnus within the family Anatidae. The swans' closest relatives include geese and ducks. Swans are grouped with the closely related geese in the subfamily Anserinae, forming the tribe Cygnini. Sometimes, they are considered a distinct subfamily, Cygninae. They are the largest waterfowl and are often among the largest flighted birds in their range."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mute_Swan_Emsworth2.JPG/330px-Mute_Swan_Emsworth2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swan","wikidata":"Q29564928"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Black_Swan_skeleton.jpg/500px-Black_Swan_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Black_Swan_skeleton.jpg/1280px-Black_Swan_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Black_Swan_skeleton.jpg/500px-Black_Swan_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Swan_skeleton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Black_Swan%2C_Burwood%2C_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_25436537_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Black_Swan%2C_Burwood%2C_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_25436537_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Black_Swan%2C_Burwood%2C_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_25436537_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Black_Swan%2C_Burwood%2C_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_25436537_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Swan%2C_Burwood%2C_Christchurch%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_25436537_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Black_Swan%2C_Warwickshire%2C_England%2C_GB_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_549760237.jpg/500px-Black_Swan%2C_Warwickshire%2C_England%2C_GB_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_549760237.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Black_Swan%2C_Warwickshire%2C_England%2C_GB_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_549760237.jpg/1280px-Black_Swan%2C_Warwickshire%2C_England%2C_GB_imported_fro